{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:faca03216e968b12","name":"Engineer (CL 2)","source":{"id":"source:reference-faca03216e968b12","title":"Engineer (CL 2)","revision":18912,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T20:57:53Z","sha256":"c7fcc0e75e2b56de777f256f5556ad1a301e4b2ce17376bbb4181954724d397c","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=18912","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Engineer%20%28CL%202%29&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-faca03216e968b12","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Threats of the Galaxy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Threats_of_the_Galaxy"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Behind every technological wonder in the galaxy is an Engineer who had the vision and expertise needed to make the impossible possible. Engineers are skilled technicians who specialize in the construction, maintenance, and modification of machines. These individuals know the ins and outs of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship"}," design, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droids","referenceId":"reference:6e72e583603b9ea8"},", and weaponry.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["In addition to the technology specialist described here, combat Engineers fill an important role in the military organizations of the galaxy. These individuals apply their technological expertise to the business of warfare. Most of them see to the assembly of powerful artillery to pound enemy forces, but others might attend to constructing bridges for foot soldiers or building breastworks, landing platforms, and barracks. Whatever a military unit needs, it's the engineer's responsibility to make it happen.\n"]},"\n\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Engineer Encounters"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Engineers are ubiquitous. The demand for new technology keeps engineers busy manufacturing new ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droids","referenceId":"reference:6e72e583603b9ea8"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starships"},", weapons, and all manner of other technological wonders. One is likely to find Engineers in the company of a wide assortment of characters, from squads of soldiers to teams of technicians arguing about how to fix the Hyperdrive computer in a dilapidated frigate.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Many technology specialists work in small teams consisting of a few peers and twice as many technicians to deal with the mundane aspects of their jobs. ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droids","referenceId":"reference:6e72e583603b9ea8"}," are also common companions for these engineers, with Construction Droids and Power Droids being the most likely. In addition, nearly every engineer employs an Astromech Droid to run diagnostics and communicate with the machine's onboard computer.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["As for combat Engineers, one or two can be found attached to a company of soldiers, though entire units of combat engineers do exist as well, such as the Combat Engineers Battalion of the Grand Army of the Republic. These Engineers are better armed and armored, and have the additional support of military personnel to give them covering fire while they work out the logistics of a problem.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Generally, though, an Engineer is not a combatant and is not likely to join a firefight. Engineers leave such engagements to the professionals. Instead, they modify gear, improve armor, and optimize ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicles"},", while working to keep support ",{"tag":"a","children":["Equipment"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Equipment","referenceId":"reference:7f2465ac7cefab27"}," in top working order.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Engineer Statistics (CL 2)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Medium ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nonheroic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nonheroic","referenceId":"reference:1bca2ef1d9ebe1c3"}," 3/",{"tag":"a","children":["Scoundrel"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scoundrel","referenceId":"reference:316d580fd4c35ecc"}," 1\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Force Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Points"},":"]}," 2\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +3; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +2\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Languages:"]}," Basic, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Binary"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Binary","referenceId":"reference:ee1c8277caf5fb9b"},", 4 Unassigned\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 16 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},": 15), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},": 12, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Will Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Will_Defense"},": 12\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Hit Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hit_Points","referenceId":"reference:58e8ee2c9538d027"},": 12, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Damage Threshold"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Damage_Threshold"},": 12\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Offense"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Speed:"]}," 6 Squares\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Melee:"]